# Commands of the terminal window's menus without a shortcut action, and
# actions whose menu command is on no menu. One line each:
#     IDM_NAME | reason
# Read by tools/check-menu-shortcuts.py. A line whose command has an action
# and a menu item, or neither, is stale and fails the build.

# the menu without an action
IDM_ABOUT | About: no key needed
IDM_HELP | Help: no key needed
IDM_QUIT | Exit: no key needed (Alt+F4 closes the window)

# actions without a menu item
IDM_NEWSESS | New Session: its menu line is hidden on purpose (window.c). The handler stays for the opennew key.
IDM_REKEY | Repeat key exchange: the menu offers it in Special Command, under an id set at run time.
